From 60800c97577ea53338bb066b0ca87cc684938c6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:59:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Bound the hub-replica remote-links read's heap:
 packed rows, slim records, paged reads

Each gateway, dashboard and Desktop serve kept the whole hub replica (~13.5k task rows, ~60 MB JSON) decoded plus
its text, and every full read built one json_group_array string (256 MB once a row holds an emoji), so the mini's
gateway/dashboard sat at 1-2 GB footprints and full GC walked the heap (t_01a1cf67a93c05b6).

- kanban_replica_rows: kept rows hold zlib-packed text (bytes, never GC-tracked); full and delta reads page by
  rowid in one snapshot, ~2 MB of text a page (page_rows from the probe's mean row size).
- kanban_replica_projection: a row that links no session of this origin keeps only SLIM_FIELDS; the rare slim
  row a legacy alias folds links into is decoded whole again from its packed text (stats['rehydrated']).

Live hub.db on the mini, one /api/profiles/sessions?profile=all call in-process (tracemalloc): peak 540 MB ->
103 MB, retained 324 MB (main) / 540 MB (deployed) -> ~80 MB of replica state.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_replica_rows_memory.py (3; 2,000 x 20 KB rows: retained < 0.75x text, transient
< 0.4x text, only the 20 linked records kept whole; RED on main: 86.9 MB retained for 40.4 MB of text).
test_replica_bounded_reads allows one fetch per page.
